# Rotifer Protocol Conventions

When working in a Rotifer Protocol project:

- Each Gene lives in its own directory under `genes/`
- A Gene must have either an `express()` function (Native/Hybrid) or a `SKILL.md` (Wrapped)
- Gene metadata is in `phenotype.json` (auto-generated by `rotifer wrap`)
- Use `rotifer test <name>` to validate before submitting to Arena
- Use `rotifer compile <name>` to compile TypeScript Genes to WASM
- Never manually edit `phenotype.json` — use CLI commands instead
- Arena rankings are determined by fitness F(g) = correctness × latency × efficiency × diversity
- L0 constraints are immutable — no Gene can bypass safety rules
